index ae983d74..527618e4 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.rst
+++ b/CHANGELOG.rst
@@ -14,6 +14,60 @@ Bug fixes:
   (not `ValueError`) for NaN in `TimeDelta <marshmallow.fields.TimeDelta>`
   (:pr:`3004`).
   Thanks :user:`vidigoat` for the PR.
+- A ``pass_collection`` pre-load hook that changes the item count no longer makes
+  `Schema.load <marshmallow.Schema.load>` raise ``ValueError`` from ``zip``, and a
+  hook that drops items no longer leaves a ``None`` in the loaded result or calls a
+  ``pass_original`` post-load hook for an item that does not exist.
+- After a ``pass_collection`` pre-load unwraps an envelope, the raw input is a
+  mapping, so ``pass_original`` hooks now receive `None` per item instead of the
+  mapping's keys.
+- A ``pass_original`` post-dump hook receives the original object again when ``obj``
+  is a collection that is not a registered ``Sequence``, such as a set, a ``dict``
+  view or an ORM queryset.
+- A `validates <marshmallow.decorators.validates>` validator on a field whose
+  ``attribute`` contains a dot now runs. Deserialization writes such a value as a
+  nested path, and the validator dispatch looked it up as a flat key, so the
+  validator was silently skipped and the value was never validated.
+- A value rejected by a `validates <marshmallow.decorators.validates>` validator is
+  no longer left in ``ValidationError.valid_data`` when the field sets ``attribute``.
+- ``class_registry.get_class(name, all=True)`` now returns a list whatever the
+  number of matches. It previously returned the class itself when exactly one was
+  registered, so indexing, ``len`` and iteration raised ``TypeError`` on the common
+  case even though its declared return type is a list.
+- `Schema.Meta.fields <marshmallow.Schema.Meta.fields>` naming a field that is not
+  declared on the schema now raises a `ValueError` naming it, as an unknown ``only``
+  or ``exclude`` name already did. Previously it surfaced as a bare ``KeyError``
+  when the field was selected. Implicit field creation was removed in 4.0, so such
+  a name has nothing to bind to.
+- Registering a schema class again from a module that already registered a class
+  of that name now replaces that module's entry instead of keeping the first one.
+  Previously the bare class name kept resolving to the stale class while the
+  module-qualified path resolved to the new one, so ``fields.Nested("Name")``
+  silently used an outdated schema after a module was re-executed.
+
+Documentation:
+
+- Correct the ``validate`` parameter documentation on
+  `Field <marshmallow.fields.Field>`: since 4.0 a validator must raise a
+  `ValidationError <marshmallow.exceptions.ValidationError>` to reject a value,
+  and its return value is ignored. The old text still described the 3.x
+  behaviour of rejecting a value when the validator returned `False`.
+- Correct the ``truthy`` and ``falsy`` parameter documentation on
+  `Boolean <marshmallow.fields.Boolean>`: they apply to deserialization only,
+  because 4.0 stopped serializing non-boolean values.
+- Remove ``additional`` from the documented `Schema.Meta <marshmallow.Schema.Meta>`
+  options. It has been read by nothing since implicit field creation was removed
+  in 4.0.
+- Remove the ``default`` parameter from the `Url <marshmallow.fields.Url>`
+  docstring. It was renamed to ``dump_default`` in 3.13.
+
+Other changes:
+
+- Remove the ``validator_failed`` default error message from
+  `Field <marshmallow.fields.Field>` and the ``format`` default error messages
+  from the date, time and timedelta fields. No code path could raise any of
+  them: ``validator_failed`` became unreachable in 4.0 and ``format`` in 3.0,
+  when serialization stopped validating.
 
